From 49a9a1d9717af32f0ca586447eca5b73cfde1661 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:19:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] robo(tests): read the three new source guards as LF, so a
 Windows checkout does not pass them blind
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

CI caught it: tests/sourceLineEndings.test.ts, added to main after this round
was started, requires every test that reads a source file as TEXT to normalise
its line endings. The three guards added with the Shift and hourly-chart
changes read the file as the checkout left it.

It matters in one direction and silently: on a CRLF working copy every \n in a
pattern misses, so an assert.match fails for a reason that has nothing to do
with the code — and worse, an assert.doesNotMatch passes without ever looking.
A guard that cannot fail is not a guard.

Only the three readers change; the assertions are the same ones.

